{
  "id": "tyson-cdc2-six-state-second-biology",
  "name": "Tyson conserved cdc2 and cyclin binding cycle",
  "description": "Explicit cdc2 phosphorylation, cyclin binding and autocatalytic preMPF activation conserve the cdc2 pool. Different mechanism from the Goldbeter three-activity cascade. Concentration scale follows the CellML source; time is minutes. Coefficients and six initial concentrations0.001 follow the corrected Physiome source; total cdc2 is0.004. Its zero k2 and k5 terms are removed algebraically. Horizon100 and Radau output step0.1 are our verification choices. https://models.physiomeproject.org/workspace/tyson_1991/rawfile/882447deebe540870a53c5971525d12208fca27b/tyson_1991.cellml Signed net-rate flows encode the stated differential equations. No clamps or resets. These educational equations are not fitted biological forecasts.",
  "source": "https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.88.16.7328",
  "reference": "Tyson (1991), Modeling the cell division cycle: cdc2 and cyclin interactions, PNAS88:7328-7332. Numerical verification: Physiome tyson_1991 revision882447deebe540870a53c5971525d12208fca27b.",
